{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/832772-storytelling-the-curse","id":832772,"title":"Storytelling the Curse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-18T14:55:48-08:00","id":832772,"title":"Storytelling the Curse","content":"would like some advise on issues of how the curse makes people act especialy in regards to what the gift &quot;Mark of the wolf&quot; can do to a victim it can cause people to be antisocial and less outgoing towards you... would like some ideas of how it can affect people and psychological reactions to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T18:40:45-08:00","id":832928,"title":"","content":"The Curse, as written, is simple. Compare the Garou's Rage against the human's Willpower. When the Willpower is less, the human will avoid contact with the Garou if at all possible. The person's subconscious is telling them that they are around a dangerous predator and need to remove themselves to safety.<br /> <br /> How exactly each human responds will depend on their nature, their surroundings, and any other relevant information for the scene. Here are some of the things I've done.<ul><li>Police watch the Garou from a distance, call in to report suspicious activity, and then wait for back up.</li> <li>Children hide behind their parents.</li> <li>People on subways give the person a wide berth.</li> <li>Extremely sick or old people in hospital beds begin crying and curl up in fetal position.</li> <li>Passersby avoid the Garou and choose another path to get the way they are going.</li> <li>People will begin acting in ways to not draw attention to themselves - they will become quiet, put barriers (even if only a menu, newspaper, or lamppole) between themselves and the Garou</li> <li>A very few will assume postures designed to make themselves look dangerous or bigger in order to make the Garou think they are too dangerous to mess with.</li> <li>If for whatever reason they cannot get away, they will act in ways that they think will prevent them from &quot;provoking&quot; the Garou and minimize contact.</li> <li>In extremely rare cases, the person becomes aggressive themselves towards the Garou</li> </ul>People react to the Garou as if they are a threat to their lives and react accordingly to them. If their willpower is lower than the Garou's rage, they think the garou is a threat. Their fight or flight response begins kicking in.<br /> <br /> They don't know WHY they feel threatened all of a sudden, and may feel it is irrational, but at that point in time their reason is being clouded by their emotional response as the brain begins telling the body to produce the appropriate stress hormones. Remember - this is a SURVIVAL reaction at the primal level.<br /> <br /> If their Willpower is equal or higher than the Garou's Rage, then technically the Curse is not operative. However, I often have lesser versions of the Curse - they think there is something dangerous to the Garou, but not that the Garou is a threat to them. This could be anything that the Garou is a jerk they hate, a potential troublemaker, or even a bad boy/girl type they are attracted to.<br /> <br /> There is a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vc2cPuwpqTg\" target=\"_blank\">scene</a> in Full Metal Jacket where &quot;Gomer Pyle&quot; has had a psychotic break, and Joker and the Drill Sergeant know he's snapped and their lives are in danger. The Garou in question would NOT be acting like Gomer Pyle. He may be acting perfectly normal. But people will be reacting similarly to Joker and the Drill Sergeant. It is not the only way the Curse can be portrayed, but it would be appropriate in some situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:22:48-08:00","id":832952,"title":"","content":"yes it becomes more problematic if the garou winds up socially interacting with the person... and doing a good job...<br /> <br /> Hmmmn some possibletys... &quot;Danger comes with allure&quot; <br /> <br /> but when your trying to reserve a hotel room...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\"