tedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/832772-storytelling-the-curse?p=842475#post842475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um. Not really. It's a very Urban Gift. And it's only on Homid lists.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;only&quot; on the most common gift list in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T15:05:19-08:00","id":843150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/832772-storytelling-the-curse?p=843133#post843133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;only&quot; on the most common gift list in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet a cursory examination of printed characters doesn't seem to have it on every published NPC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T15:36:45-08:00","id":843162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/832772-storytelling-the-curse?p=843150#post843150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet a cursory examination of printed characters doesn't seem to have it on every published NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how well statted the NPCs (or templates) can be, I honestly am not surprised. There is a Wendigo Lupus Theurge template in the revised book with only streetwise and subterfuge in its talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T16:06:47-08:00","id":843170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/832772-storytelling-the-curse?p=843162#post843162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering how well statted the NPCs (or templates) can be, I honestly am not surprised. There is a Wendigo Lupus Theurge template in the revised book with only streetwise and subterfuge in its talents.</div> </div> </div> </div>... that's True.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T21:54:04-08:00","id":845460,"title":"","content":"The Curse is rarely used by STs because they don't know how to move most stories forward when every NPC treats the PCs suspiciously, or with fear/aggression. It's a great reason to include Kinfolk, as well as to keep the game away from the mundane--you can't have a game delayed with &quot;let's go shopping for pants/skirts/clothing&quot; when the shop owners keep closing their doors on you, or refuse you service. Your PC can't spend their downtime &quot;working at Burger King&quot; or even running their own bar when the customers won't stick around to order, let alone trying to work around normal folks.<br /> <br /> It's one of the reasons why one's First Change is so terrible--before it even really starts, that Rage begins to manifest, boiling out and protruding. Friends no longer want to be around you, teachers and superiors treat you with hostility, family won't open their doors to you as you try to find help. You're shunned by society at an already immensely awkward time for anyone let alone as these new urges, feelings, senses begin to creep into your young mind and body in ways that don't fit into any sexual education booklet (<i>eating my burgers and steak raw is just natural, you know? What do you mean that's not normal?</i>) And it's at the peak of that time that you suddenly manifest, your soul is consumed by fire and you are reborn into a Garou with a whole new awareness. Hopefully there is someone there to make sense of it for you and guide you into the Garou Nation before you go uncontrolled, or (worse) found and brought into the maddened embrace of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> This is the reason Kinfolk are so important to the Garou--the Kinfolk are the means by which most Garou interact and get things from Mundane society. Kinfolk are the ones who go into the city, talk to the cops, do the work in public, so that the Garou can focus on the real task at hand--saving the world from the supernatural Evil that wants to tear it all apart in the most vile and fearsome ways possible.<br /> <br /> Even for the Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers have trouble with this and either must find ways of working around it, or through it.<br /> <br /> As a player, I want my Storyteller to really use The Curse to keep the story directed towards the supernatural and away from the mundane--if we're going to be dealing with the mundane world, it's likely as the Monster we are, not as the people we're no longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T16:14:14-07:00","id":846775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/832772-storytelling-the-curse?p=845460#post845460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a player, I want my Storyteller to really use The Curse to keep the story directed towards the supernatural and away from the mundane--if we're going to be dealing with the mundane world, it's likely as the Monster we are, not as the people we're no longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>*nods*<br /> I would point out that even with all of that said, there's a whole butt-load of stuff that the Garou still need from human society, so if the characters don't <i>have</i> Kinfolk readily available (or have been doing their level best to alienate them), the Curse is a good tool to use when illustrating that. If the local city council is debating letting a Pentex subsidiary move in and set up a chemical plant because it will bring back jobs that its industrial base has lost over the last four decades -- fangs and claws aren't so useful anymore. Influential Kinfolk are.<br /> <br /> Also, Garou tend to be pretty dismissive of &quot;mere&quot; humans. Trying to subtly stake out said Pentex plant when every cop on the beat automatically zeros in on the characters, tends to illustrate why that dismissive mindset is often unhelpful.<br /> <br /> Slightly off topic: We did a game in which we came up with house rules for <i>using</i> the Curse (as in, <i>observing</i> its <i>effects</i> in ordinary humans on the street) as a way for a sniper to figure out who in a crowd was Garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T18:06:02-07:00","id":846835,"title":"","content":"Good Points, Two things, On the &quot;Shopping for Clothes&quot; I HAVE Done that in downtime, a time or two, think most garou who want clothes will shop on Amazon a lot, to avoid having to deal with people.<br /> <br /> the Gift StareDown, and a few other &quot;Fear Causing&quot; Gifts, how you think a person would react at feeling spooked by a seemingly unremarkable man glaring at them? especialy a police officer being scared by a bum, or high school girl?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T00:08:07-07:00","id":846957,"title":"","content":"Using a fear-inducing gift on a cop is a particularly bad idea. There is no (really plausible) way that that will end well. Either the cop is going to call for a <i>ton</i> of back-up and try to detain the Garou, or if it works<i> really </i>&quot;well&quot; (I guess), the cop in question is probably going to empty his service weapon into the Garou. Either way, that's probably going to be a dead cop, or a <i>lot</i> of dead cops (if his reinforcements show up). Basically a huge-normous <i>intentional</i> Veil-breach by the Garou bone-headed enough to try it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T06:57:31-07:00","id":851717,"title":"","content":"oh one more thing I just remembered? In answer to the statement that garou will never take vacations saw a little excerpt in a &quot;Session idea&quot; Involving a pack babysitting for a kinfolk... <br /> <br /> Garou and kids.. dont mix very well I t